tasks:
  - name: Update configs
    template:
      src: app.conf.j2
      dest: /etc/myapp/app.conf
    notify:
      - Restart App
      - Restart Database

  - name: Apply configs immediately
    meta: flush_handlers

  - name: Continue with deployment
    command: /usr/local/bin/myapp deploy

handlers:
  - name: Restart App
    service:
      name: myapp
      state: restarted

  - name: Restart Database
    service:
      name: postgresql
      state: restarted

##Note
Great choice— is one of those advanced Ansible features that makes handlers much more powerful. Normally, handlers run at the end of a play, but sometimes you need them to execute immediately after being notified. That’s exactly what  does.
